  "full_text": "I'm gonna eat an apple because I need an apple. Hey, Dad's back. Dad's back. Did you just get these off the tree? Are there more of them? I think that's the tree. Sunshine. So I kept biting my lip. Like... the hamburger was really good and then like pleasures and pains balance so like uh stay away from those uh that picnic was a bad idea um because those sweets and stuff maybe this is good so i kept biting my lip i couldn't believe it so uh so i was eating the spaghetti really fast and i was like biting my lip and uh Then I got to thinking, maybe you're supposed to savor it. And there's grace if you, oh my God, I just broke that. I stepped on it, broke it. So maybe there's grace in like proper table manners and stuff. Like if you eat, like sitting correctly, then the discipline of holding your posture and all that. Maybe that offsets the food pleasure. I think if I was eating fast, that's what made me bite my lip. You're supposed to slow down and savor it. It's not quite pleasures and pains. Something slightly different.",
